ively; to give up as hopeless or inevitable.","example":"He had no choice but to resign the game and let his opponent become the champion.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["quit"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["resignable","resignation","resignatory","resignee","resigner","resignful","resignment","resign oneself","unresign"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resign#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:534f29e443e8d11e3e","definition":"Alternative spelling of re-sign.","example":"Lastly, a note that I have resigned my GPG key to extend the expiration date.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of, alternative, proscribed","register":"alt-of, alternative, proscribed","wordFamily":["resignable","resignation","resignatory","resignee","resigner","resignful","resignment","resign oneself","unresign"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resign#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɹɪˈzaɪn/"},"wordFamily":["resignable","resignation","resignatory","resignee","resigner","resignful","resignment","resign oneself","unresign"]}